            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-08T07:00:15.837599+00:00",
            "notes": "Pharah's weakness is always sustain, especially with a high movement speed build it makes it harder for your healers to heal you. Going life steal is a must, and by round 3 we will be sitting on the 3 life steal items for a while.\n\n[Cairo Coolant](item_201118c4-cd0f-43ca-9e7e-51e66be10d9a) is not THAT good, but it keeps us moving until level 5. Speed is important, and you will feel like at level 3. We are preparing so the later rounds are fully damage maxed\n\nI like running [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) but living is always more important than damage. Life steal goes through armor (aka does not give you less healing) so stacking armor with [Vital-E-Tee](item_b92e6f1d-3aac-4eec-b027-00c8e1529016) is good. \n\nIf you are constantly dying, getting [Emergency Chip](item_c73e060f-94df-4e6b-bb6d-fe2f65e31dd1) is also good. Remember, only if you are dying a lot, if you are getting low a lot but not dying, this will NOT help.\n\n[Cushioned Padding](item_20f2f4bc-4611-4d1f-b653-20f04d56b96f) is VERY good if they have an ana running [Tranquilizer](item_2bea20a0-21c0-4a52-b81e-596c17d184b4). Ana WILL run this if they are running [Sleep Regimen](item_28934e4f-0668-482e-b10d-a5d557cc3b1e) as they want to be spamming sleep consistantly",
